@*
    One open impediment in the stand-up (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md#the-stand-up):
    its title, a state picker wearing the state's badge, and one line naming who it is
    with, its age in working days or the day to check it again, and the goal it holds
    back in color-error-text — "Account manager · 3 days · Customers get paid faster".

    The picker is a BadgeSelect of the impediment family, toned per
    .devbook/design/color-scheme.md#impediment-state-tones, and offers the stored state
    and the moves the host says it may make — forward only, and any open state to
    Resolved — so a refused move is rare. When one is refused anyway the host keeps the
    stored state and says why, and the picker shows the stored state again rather than
    the one the person picked. It does so on the same select, never a new one, so a
    keyboard user's focus stays where it was: the row renders the picked value once
    and then the stored one, and that change in the rendered value is what makes
    Blazor write the stored value back onto the element. Re-keying the select would
    write it too, by replacing the element, and drop the focus to the page.

    Under the meta line the row shows the impediment's note — the one the phone's
    impediment page writes too — wrapped as written. With a host listening, an
    "Add note" or "Edit note" button opens the note in place as a text box: leaving the
    box or Ctrl+Enter hands the text back trimmed, a blank one as none, and Escape
    abandons it. There is no Save button (interaction-guidelines.md#auto-save-no-save-buttons),
    the Escape stops at the box (#task-rows, "Escape belongs to the innermost draft"),
    and an unchanged note is not handed back. Closed by a key, the focus goes back to the
    button; left by Tab or a click, it stays where the person took it. The box has no
    visible label, so a click on one cannot blur it shut. Without a host the note is
    text alone, never an inert control.

    Once everything the impediment holds back is settled, a "Ready to resolve" badge in the
    settled tone sits beside the picker (.devbook/domain/progress/features.md
    #seeing-an-impediment-ready-to-resolve): a reading the person acts on, never a state,
    so the picker still holds the stored one and resolving stays the person's.

    Under the note the row lists what it holds back, in the order linked, each under its
    kind label — Task, PR, Plan — and, with a host listening on OnUnlink, an icon-only
    Unlink named for the item (#linking-what-an-impediment-holds-back). Unlinking changes
    nothing on the work, so it does not ask. With a host listening on OnLink, "Link…" opens
    the work search (WorkItemSearch) under it, limited to tasks, pull requests and plans
    and leaving out what the row already holds; a pick hands the item back and the search
    stays open for the next, and Link… or Escape closes it, the focus back on Link…. A
    refusal shows under the search in the module's words (LinkError).
*@
@inject IJSRuntime Js
<div class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId" data-state="@Slug(Impediment.State)">
    <div class="impediment-row__head">
        <span class="impediment-row__title">@Impediment.Title</span>
        @if (Impediment.ReadyToResolve)
        {
            <Badge Kind="tone" Slug="settled" CssClass="impediment-row__ready" TestId="@Part("ready")">@GoalsText.ReadyToResolve</Badge>
        }
        <BadgeSelect Id="@_pickerId"
                     CurrentValue="@Shown.ToString()"
                     Options="Options"
                     Label="State"
                     BadgeKind="impediment"
                     Slug="@Slug(Shown)"
                     Disabled="@(Disabled || Impediment.Moves.Count == 0)"
                     OnChanged="MoveAsync"
                     TestId="@Part("state")" />
    </div>
    <span class="impediment-row__meta" data-testid="@Part("meta")">
        @GoalsText.ImpedimentMeta(Impediment)
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Impediment.GoalTitle))
        {
            <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
            <span class="impediment-row__goal">@Impediment.GoalTitle</span>
        }
    </span>
    @if (_editing)
    {
        <div class="impediment-row__note-editor" @onkeydown="NoteKeyAsync" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="true" @onfocusout="CommitAsync">
            <TextArea Id="@_noteId"
                      AriaLabel="@($"Note on {Impediment.Title}")"
                      Placeholder="Note"
                      Value="@_draft"
                      ValueChanged="value => _draft = value"
                      Rows="2"
                      TestId="@Part("note-editor")" />
        </div>
    }
    else if (ShownNote is not null || CanEdit)
    {
        <div class="impediment-row__note-line">
            @if (ShownNote is { } note)
            {
                <p class="impediment-row__note" data-testid="@Part("note")">@note</p>
            }
            @if (CanEdit)
            {
                <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                           Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                           Disabled="Disabled"
                           Busy="_saving"
                           BusyLabel="Saving the note"
                           CssClass="impediment-row__note-edit"
                           OnClick="OpenNote"
                           TestId="@Part("note-edit")"
                           id="@_noteButtonId"
                           aria-label="@($"{(ShownNote is null ? "Add note to" : "Edit note on")} {Impediment.Title}")">@(ShownNote is null ? "Add note" : "Edit note")</AppButton>
            }
        </div>
    }
    @if (Impediment.HoldsBack.Count > 0)
    {
        <ul class="impediment-row__items" aria-label="@($"What {Impediment.Title} holds back")" data-testid="@Part("items")">
            @foreach (var item in Impediment.HoldsBack)
            {
                <li class="impediment-row__item" data-kind="@WorkItemSearch.KindLabel(item.Kind)" data-testid="@Part($"item-{item.Subject.Key}")">
                    <span class="impediment-row__item-kind">@WorkItemSearch.KindLabel(item.Kind)</span>
                    <span class="impediment-row__item-title">@WorkItemSearch.Line(item)</span>
                    @if (CanUnlink)
                    {
                        <IconButton AriaLabel="@($"Unlink {WorkItemSearch.Line(item)} from {Impediment.Title}")"
                                    Title="Unlink"
                                    Disabled="Disabled"
                                    CssClass="impediment-row__unlink"
                                    OnClick="() => UnlinkAsync(item.Subject)"
                                    TestId="@Part($"unlink-{item.Subject.Key}")">
                            <XIcon Size="14" />
                        </IconButton>
                    }
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    }
    @if (CanLink)
    {
        <div class="impediment-row__link" @onkeydown="LinkKey" @onkeydown:stopPropagation="_linking">
            <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Ghost"
                       Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                       Disabled="Disabled"
                       CssClass="impediment-row__link-toggle"
                       OnClick="ToggleLink"
                       TestId="@Part("link")"
                       id="@_linkButtonId"
                       aria-expanded="@(_linking ? "true" : "false")"
                       aria-label="@($"Link work to {Impediment.Title}")">Link…</AppButton>
            @if (_linking)
            {
                <WorkItemSearch @ref="_search"
                                Kinds="WorkItemSearch.ImpedimentKinds"
                                Candidates="Candidates"
                                Excluding="@([.. Impediment.HoldsBack.Select(item => item.Subject)])"
                                Repositories="Repositories"
                                Label="@LinkLabel"
                                AriaLabel="@($"{LinkLabel} to {Impediment.Title}")"
                                OnPick="match => LinkAsync(match.Subject)"
                                CssClass="impediment-row__search"
                                TestId="@Part("link-search")"
                                SearchTestId="@Part("link-search-box")" />
            }
            <Alert Message="@LinkError" TestId="@Part("link-error")" />
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    private readonly string _pickerId = "impediment-state-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private readonly string _noteId = "impediment-note-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private readonly string _noteButtonId = "impediment-note-edit-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private StandUpImpedimentState? _picked;
    private bool _editing;
    private bool _saving;
    private string _draft = string.Empty;
    private string? _sent;
    private string? _focus;
    private readonly string _linkButtonId = "impediment-link-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");
    private bool _linking;
    private bool _focusSearch;
    private WorkItemSearch? _search;

    /// <summary>The Link… search's placeholder.</summary>
    public const string LinkLabel = "Link a task, pull request or plan";

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public StandUpImpediment Impediment { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>A state was picked; the host saves the move and reads the view again.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<StandUpImpedimentState> OnMove { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The note was written; the host saves it and reads the view again. Null
    /// clears it. Without a listener the note is shown and cannot be edited.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string?> OnEditNote { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A task, pull request or plan was picked in the Link… search; the host links
    /// it and reads the view again. Without a listener there is no Link….</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalSubject> OnLink { get; set; }

    /// <summary>An item's Unlink was pressed; the host unlinks it and reads the view again.
    /// Without a listener no item has one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<GoalSubject> OnUnlink { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What the Link… search matches over.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<GoalsItem> Candidates { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The repositories a bare pull request number in the Link… search is read in.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Repositories { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>Why the last link or unlink was refused, in the module's words.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? LinkError { get; set; }

    /// <summary>While a move is being saved.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Lands on the row; the picker and the meta line take it as a prefix.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Puts the focus on the row's state picker, by its id, through the library's
    /// focus helper — so BadgeSelect's markup stays what every other caller renders.</summary>
    public Task FocusAsync() => global::Backlog.UI.Components.Tasks.QuickEditField.FocusAsync(Js, _pickerId, select: false);

    /// <summary>The picked state while its move is being saved, the stored one otherwise.</summary>
    private StandUpImpedimentState Shown => _picked ?? Impediment.State;

    private bool CanEdit => OnEditNote.HasDelegate;

    private bool CanLink => OnLink.HasDelegate;

    private bool CanUnlink => OnUnlink.HasDelegate;

    private void ToggleLink()
    {
        _linking = !_linking;
        if (_linking) _focusSearch = true;
        else _focus = _linkButtonId;
    }

    /// <summary>Escape closes the search and stops there, the focus back on Link….</summary>
    private void LinkKey(KeyboardEventArgs key)
    {
        if (!_linking || key.Key != "Escape") return;

        _linking = false;
        _focus = _linkButtonId;
    }

    private Task LinkAsync(GoalSubject subject) => OnLink.InvokeAsync(subject);

    /// <summary>Hands the item back. Its line goes with the reading, so the focus waits on
    /// Link… when there is one; a refused unlink leaves the line and the focus on its
    /// Unlink.</summary>
    private async Task UnlinkAsync(GoalSubject subject)
    {
        await OnUnlink.InvokeAsync(subject);
        await Task.Yield();

        if (CanLink && Impediment.HoldsBack.All(item => item.Subject != subject)) _focus = _linkButtonId;
    }

    /// <summary>The note handed back while it is being saved, the stored one otherwise.</summary>
    private string? ShownNote => _saving ? _sent : Clean(Impediment.Note);

    private string ClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? "impediment-row" : $"impediment-row {CssClass}";

    private string? Part(string part) => TestId is null ? null : $"{TestId}-{part}";

    /// <summary>The stored state, then its moves, in the state order.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<SelectorOption> Options =>
    [
        .. new[] { Impediment.State }
            .Concat(Impediment.Moves.Where(state => state != Impediment.State))
            .Order()
            .Select(state => new SelectorOption(state.ToString(), GoalsText.State(state)))
    ];

    /// <summary>The badge slug a state wears: <c>new</c>, <c>being-handled</c>.</summary>
    public static string Slug(StandUpImpedimentState state) => state switch
    {
        StandUpImpedimentState.BeingHandled => "being-handled",
        _ => state.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()
    };

    private async Task MoveAsync(string value)
    {
        if (!Enum.TryParse<StandUpImpedimentState>(value, out var state) || state == Impediment.State) return;

        // Render the pick first, so the render after the move differs from it wherever the
        // host kept the stored state, and the stored value is written back onto the select.
        _picked = state;
        StateHasChanged();
        await Task.Yield();

        try
        {
            await OnMove.InvokeAsync(state);
        }
        finally
        {
            _picked = null;
        }
    }

    private void OpenNote()
    {
        _draft = Impediment.Note ?? string.Empty;
        _editing = true;
        _focus = _noteId;
    }

    private async Task NoteKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs key)
    {
        if (key.Key == "Escape")
        {
            Close(refocus: true);
        }
        else if (key.Key == "Enter" && key.CtrlKey)
        {
            await CommitAsync(refocus: true);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Hands the draft back unless it says what the note says, and closes the box.
    /// The box closing may raise its own focusout; once closed that one finds nothing. Left
    /// by focusout, the focus is wherever the person took it; closed by a key, it goes back
    /// to the button.</summary>
    private Task CommitAsync() => CommitAsync(refocus: false);

    private async Task CommitAsync(bool refocus)
    {
        if (!_editing) return;

        var note = Clean(_draft);
        Close(refocus);
        if (string.Equals(note, Clean(Impediment.Note), StringComparison.Ordinal)) return;

        _sent = note;
        _saving = true;
        try
        {
            await OnEditNote.InvokeAsync(note);
        }
        finally
        {
            _saving = false;
            _sent = null;
        }
    }

    private void Close(bool refocus)
    {
        _editing = false;
        _draft = string.Empty;
        if (refocus) _focus = _noteButtonId;
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (_focusSearch && _search is not null)
        {
            // Link… opened the search: the focus goes into its box.
            _focusSearch = false;
            await _search.FocusAsync();
        }

        if (_focus is not { } id) return;

        _focus = null;
        await global::Backlog.UI.Components.Tasks.QuickEditField.FocusAsync(Js, id, select: false);
    }

    private static string? Clean(string? text) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(text) ? null : text.Trim();
}
